  "principles": [
    "No direct self-modification from a single low-severity observation.",
    "Add or strengthen an eval that represents the failure before changing routing/procedure when practical.",
    "Use the smallest change that addresses the observed failure.",
    "Always snapshot the harness before a candidate mutation.",
    "Reject candidates that improve one case by causing material regressions elsewhere.",
    "High-risk harness boundaries require human review before promotion."
